SUMMARY:Caledon's Culture Days Providence Cemetery Tour
DESCRIPTION:On Saturday\, October 3rd\, as part of the Town of Caledon’s Culture Days and a part of a national celebration the Providence Cemetery Board is hosting a Guided Walking Tour of Providence Cemetery\, at 14580 Innis Lake Road\, Caledon\, Ont. starting at 1:00PM – 2:30PM. \nNathan Hiller will take you back in time and explore the rich history of Providence Cemetery on a free guided walking tour. Discover the stories of Caledon’s early settlers\, learn about the community’s heritage\, and uncover the fascinating history behind the cemetery’s historic monuments and markers. This engaging tour offers a unique opportunity to connect with the people and places that helped shape Caledon’s past. Whether you’re a history enthusiast\, interested in local heritage\, or simply looking for a unique Culture Days experience\, this tour is sure to inspire. \nhttps://culturedays.ca/en/events/5a9200ed-af89-45a2-9e96-365b2d3a586f \nRegistration is not required. Rain or Shine. No washrooms are available on site. \nCome celebrate Caledon’s history and heritage with us during Culture Days. You can find other local and provincial events at https://culturedays.ca/en/events/map?bb=38.61%2C-95.86%2C50.13%2C-61.14 \nQuestions please contact Nathan at 905-584-2801
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/caledons-culture-days-providence-cemetery-tour/
LOCATION:Providence Cemetery\, 14580 Innis Lake Road\, Caledon\, Ontario\, L7C 2Y8\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="Albion Bolton Historical Society":MAILTO:nhillerphoto@bell.net
END:VEVENT
