SUMMARY:Free Virtual History Lectures with the Diefenbunker: Canada's Cold War Museum
DESCRIPTION:We invite you to join virtually us this fall for the Diefenbunker Museum’s 5th annual Cold War Speaker Series! In this series of free events\, you will hear from experts sharing insights into Canada’s Cold War history. \nAll lectures are free to attend\, and open to all! Advance registration is required to receive the Zoom link and the recording after the event. \nThursday\, October 15\, at 7:00 p.m. ET  \nCanadian Intelligence in the Early Cold War: Assessing the Soviet Threat to North America  \nAlan Barnes\, analyst in the Canadian intelligence community\, will speak to Canadian foreign intelligence organizations’ Cold War assessments of the Soviet threat to North America. He will also discuss the role of intelligence in decisions on the CF-105 Avro Arrow project. \n  \n 
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/free-virtual-history-lectures-with-the-diefenbunker-canadas-cold-war-museum-3/
LOCATION:online
GEO:56.130366;-106.346771
END:VEVENT
